.TH SFE 1 2026-11-15 "sfe 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sfe \- Simple File Explorer, a small file manager for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sfe
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fIDIRECTORY\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sfe
is a minimal GTK3 file manager: a sidebar with places, bookmarks, drives
and a folder tree; up to three split views in a grid or a list; fuzzy
search; thumbnails; copy, move, trash, undo and batch rename; custom
commands; and vim-style keys with a command line.
.PP
Each \fIDIRECTORY\fR opens in a window of its own; without one, a window
opens on the configured start folder. A second \fBsfe\fR hands its
windows to the one already running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options, including the standard GTK and GApplication ones.
.SH KEYS
In the file views single keys are commands (normal mode):
\fBj\fR/\fBk\fR move, \fBh\fR goes to the parent folder, \fBl\fR opens,
\fBv\fR selects with the keyboard, \fByy\fR/\fBdd\fR/\fBp\fR copy, cut and
paste, \fBu\fR undoes, \fB/\fR searches and \fB:\fR opens the command line.
Ctrl+W followed by \fBv\fR, \fBs\fR or \fBq\fR splits and closes views.
After half a second in a key chord, sfe lists the keys that can follow.
.PP
The usual shortcuts work too: Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+V, Ctrl+Z, Delete, F2,
Ctrl+F, Ctrl+H (hidden files), Ctrl+S (sidebar), Ctrl+P (settings).
Every key is listed in the user guide and can be changed in the settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sfe/config.toml
Settings, keys, custom commands and programs per file type. Created with
comments on first start; reloaded whenever it changes. Errors are reported
as desktop notifications.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css
The GTK user stylesheet; sfe reloads it (and the colour files it imports)
when it changes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks
GTK bookmarks, shown in the sidebar.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/thumbnails
Thumbnails, shared with other file managers (freedesktop.org thumbnail
specification).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Trash
The trash.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/sfe/guide/index.md
The user guide.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=sfe
Log what sfe does to standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR udisksctl (1)
.PP
The user guide: \fI/usr/share/doc/sfe/guide/index.md\fR, or
https://github.com/dakata1337/sfe/blob/main/docs/guide/index.md
